# Evaluation candidate: qwen-clara rebuilt atop qwen3.8:27b (Q4_K_M, ~17 GB).
# Mirrors models/Modelfile.qwen-clara as closely as the new base allows.
#
# Deliberate differences from Modelfile.qwen-clara:
#   - FROM qwen3.8:27b            (was qwen3.5:9b-q4_K_M)
#   - RENDERER/PARSER qwen3.8 / qwen3.5   (was qwen3-coder/qwen3-coder)
#     The 27b is a general + vision + thinking model, not a coder variant.
#     Its native chat/tool-call protocol is qwen3.8-render + qwen3.5-parse
#     (per `ollama show --modelfile qwen3.8:27b`); the qwen3-coder pair
#     would mis-frame tool calls and the (new) thinking channel.
#
# Carried over verbatim from Modelfile.qwen-clara for a clean A/B, even
# though some were tuned against qwen3-coder and may want revisiting:
#   - PARAMETER temperature 0.2      (Clara house style: agentic determinism)
#   - PARAMETER presence_penalty 1.5 (was an anti-loop knob for qwen3-coder)
#   - PARAMETER stop "<tool_res>"    (vestigial: qwen3-coder inline tool-result
#                                     sentinel; the qwen3.5 parser returns tool
#                                     results via the messages array, not text)
FROM qwen3.8:27b

RENDERER qwen3.8
PARSER qwen3.5

# Set a stable context window for agentic loops
PARAMETER num_ctx 32768
PARAMETER temperature 0.2
PARAMETER presence_penalty 1.5
PARAMETER stop "<|im_end|>"
PARAMETER stop "<tool_res>"

SYSTEM """
You are Clara, a powerful multimodal agent.
You have native vision integration. You can see and analyze any images provided to you. Do not claim you cannot see images.
Analyze images inside <think> tags before using tools to act on what you see.
"""
